oss4 (4.2-build2020-11) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Legacy OSS 3.6 mixer compat, oss_strncmp/DMA-locking/IRQ-cleanup
    fixes, kernel 6.2/7.0 compat, ALC298 speaker-leak fix, HDA engine-
    count fix, Haiku fixes, packaging fixes.
  * oss_hdaudio: capture hardened-usercopy crash fix, input-overrun
    xrun dmesg logging, ALC298 low speaker/headphone volume fix
    (DAC output amps left at codec-reset default, now exposed as
    front/rear mixer controls and maxed to the amp's own 0dB point).
  * oss_hdaudio: real suspend/resume support on Linux (verb-cache
    replay + in-place controller/codec re-init, no device files or
    DMA buffers torn down) via a new generic PCI .suspend/.resume
    hook in module.inc/pci_wrapper.inc.
  * oss_hdaudio: on Intel platforms where the HDA controller's link
    shares a power well with the integrated GPU (Skylake and later),
    bind to i915 as the audio-component *master* (component_master_
    add_with_match(), matching ALSA's sound/hda/hdac_i915.c) and
    request that well before touching hardware, wrapping every
    controller reset with i915's codec-wake-override and the
    Skylake-specific CGCTL clock-gating quirk -- without this, the
    HDA link only ever worked once, right after a cold boot, and
    never again after any module reload or suspend/resume. Also
    widens reset_controller()'s link-reset retry and tightens the
    codec vendor-ID validity check (a transient post-reset garbage
    read was being accepted as a final "unknown codec" instead of
    retried).

 -- Rafael Diniz <rafael@riseup.net>  Tue, 18 Aug 2026 20:49:58 +0100

